<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Gaixia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/202-bce">202 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chu-han-contention">Chu–Han Contention</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Gaixia, fought in 202 BCE in what is now Anhui province, was the final battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chu-han-contention">Chu–Han Contention</a>. Han forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> and his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xin">Han Xin</a> surrounded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>, whose troops, hearing Chu songs sung in the enemy camp, believed their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> lost. Xiang Yu broke out but killed himself at the Wu River, and Liu Bang founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>.</p></div>
